# Skip Blocked → Continue (cookapp) — HARD RULE

Owner rule (2026-09-18): **do not stall the whole run on one blocker.**

## When something is stuck

Treat as **blocked** and **skip for now** if any of:

- External quota / rate limit (e.g. Figma MCP daily cap)
- Stage / Gate not authorized yet (e.g. Admin §14 IA, iOS business UI)
- Waiting on Owner secrets (see `owner-config-nonblocking.mdc`)
- Waiting on Owner decision / environment (e.g. iOS Build deferred)
- Dependency Issue/PR not mergeable for reasons outside this agent's control

**Do not** sit idle, poll forever, or refuse to continue other work because of the above.

## Required behavior

1. **Skip** the blocked item (leave a short note on the Issue/PR if useful).
2. **Continue** with the next actionable item that is not blocked.
3. When the current actionable queue is drained (or at a natural checkpoint), **summarize remaining blockers** for Owner — what is stuck, why, and what decision/input is needed.
4. Owner will then say how to handle the blocked list; only then resume those items.

## Examples

| Blocked | Continue with |
|--------|----------------|
| Figma Education quota for #10 pixel rebuild | Other Issues, docs sync, Admin Gate-allowed work, triage |
| Stage-4 blocks Admin hierarchical IA | Keep flat nav; Backend APIs already on main; Integrations |
| Owner iOS Build/Test deferred | Ship code + Ready PR; do not claim Build PASS |
| Owner Config `todo` secrets | Placeholders; other modules |

## Anti-patterns

- Stopping the whole agent because one tool/quota failed
- Asking Owner mid-flight to unblock before finishing other work
- Inventing Gate-blocked UI to “keep busy”
- Marking blocked work as done without evidence
